# Revisions git blame should look through rather than at.
#
# A bulk reformat rewrites lines without changing what they do, so it makes
# `git blame` name the wrong author and the wrong date for every line it
# touched. Listing the commit here restores the answer to "who last changed
# what this line MEANS".
#
# IT IS NOT AUTOMATIC. git only reads this file when the reader has set
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# per clone. Unset, blame behaves as though this file did not exist — nothing
# breaks, the answers are just worse. GitHub's blame view applies it by default.
# The setting is documented in docs/REFACTOR-STANDARDS.txt.
#
# One SHA per line, full length. Add only commits that changed no behaviour.

